#: src/app/[locale]/long/page.tsx:10
#: src/app/[locale]/long/page.tsx:32
msgid "Field notes on shipping translations"
msgstr ""

#: src/app/[locale]/long/page.tsx:11
msgid ""
"A deliberately long page: many messages, long paragraphs, plurals, context "
"and markup, all compiled away."
msgstr ""

#: src/app/[locale]/long/page.tsx:34
msgid ""
"Everything on this page is a compiled message. There is no catalog behind "
"it, no lookup at request time, and no formatter parsing anything in the "
"browser. If you are reading this in Chinese, the Chinese text below was "
"chosen by a ternary that the compiler wrote, and in a static-locale build "
"even the ternary is gone."
msgstr ""

#: src/app/[locale]/long/page.tsx:41
msgid "Why the source text is the message"
msgstr ""

#: src/app/[locale]/long/page.tsx:43
msgid ""
"A key like home.hero.subtitle is a pointer into a file somewhere else, and "
"every pointer can dangle. When the text itself is the identifier there is "
"nothing to keep in sync: renaming a variable does not orphan a translation, "
"and a reviewer reading the diff sees the words that will actually render."
msgstr ""

#: src/app/[locale]/long/page.tsx:50
msgid ""
"The cost of that choice is honesty about what a change means. Fixing a typo "
"in the source text is a new message, because the old string was the id. The "
"catalog carries the old translation over marked fuzzy, a translator "
"confirms it, and the history stays visible instead of being silently "
"rewritten."
msgstr ""

#: src/app/[locale]/long/page.tsx:57
msgid ""
"{library} stores those messages in {format} files, because the tooling "
"translators already use has spoken that format for thirty years. Nothing "
"about the pipeline is proprietary: msgid in, msgstr out, and every "
"intermediate state survives a round trip through a TMS."
msgstr ""

#: src/app/[locale]/long/page.tsx:64
msgid "What a long paragraph compiles to"
msgstr ""

#: src/app/[locale]/long/page.tsx:66
msgid ""
"This paragraph is intentionally much longer than anything a landing page "
"would carry, because the point of this page is volume. It keeps going for "
"several sentences, the way documentation prose actually does, so that the "
"extracted catalog contains realistic entries rather than toy strings. Line "
"breaks in the source template collapse to single spaces at compile time, "
"which means re-indenting this file will never orphan the translation you "
"are reading right now."
msgstr ""

#: src/app/[locale]/long/page.tsx:75
msgid ""
"Rendered from a Server Component, all of this text reaches the browser as "
"HTML and costs exactly zero bytes of client JavaScript. The measured number "
"from the twin playgrounds: three hundred extra server-rendered messages "
"added nothing to the client bundle at all."
msgstr ""

#: src/app/[locale]/long/page.tsx:82
msgid "Plurals without a formatter"
msgstr ""

#: src/app/[locale]/long/page.tsx:84
msgid ""
"Each locale's plural formula is inlined at the call site. English has two "
"forms, Chinese has one, Russian would have three - and the compiled code "
"for a one-form locale is just the bare string."
msgstr ""

#: src/app/[locale]/long/page.tsx:90
msgid "You have one message."
msgid_plural "You have {n} messages."
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""

#: src/app/[locale]/long/page.tsx:94
msgid "Context when the same word must differ"
msgstr ""

#: src/app/[locale]/long/page.tsx:96
msgid ""
"Two identical source texts that translate differently are two different "
"messages, keyed by gettext's msgctxt:"
msgstr ""

#: src/app/[locale]/long/page.tsx:104
msgid "Markup stays out of the translator's way"
msgstr ""

#: src/app/[locale]/long/page.tsx:106
msgid ""
"A sentence can hold <strong>bold text</strong> and a{0}<a>link</a> at once, "
"and the translator still only ever sees named placeholders - never a JSX "
"attribute, never an import, never a prop."
msgstr ""

#: src/app/[locale]/long/page.tsx:114
msgid ""
"What ships is the markup itself, rebuilt per locale at build time - there "
"is <em>no component</em> walking a message tree on every render."
msgstr ""

#: src/app/[locale]/long/page.tsx:121
msgid "The workflow at volume"
msgstr ""

#: src/app/[locale]/long/page.tsx:123
msgid ""
"Extraction scans the source, writes the template, and merges each locale's "
"catalog without ever reducing the number of translations - if a run would "
"shrink a catalog, it refuses and asks for an explicit force flag. On a page "
"like this one, that guard is the difference between a refactor and an "
"accident."
msgstr ""

#: src/app/[locale]/long/page.tsx:130
msgid ""
"Validation runs both at merge time and at build time. A translation that "
"drops a placeholder, invents one, or supplies the wrong number of plural "
"forms is an error naming the file, the locale and the message - before "
"anything reaches a user."
msgstr ""

#: src/app/[locale]/long/page.tsx:136
msgid ""
"Fuzzy entries do not build. They fall back to the base locale and are "
"reported as missing, which sounds strict until the alternative is shipping "
"a stale translation under a reworded source."
msgstr ""

#: src/app/[locale]/long/page.tsx:141
msgid "What this page proves"
msgstr ""

#: src/app/[locale]/long/page.tsx:143
msgid ""
"If every heading and paragraph above renders in your language, then roughly "
"fifty messages - including this one - survived extraction, merging, "
"translation and compilation in one pass. The client bundle for this route "
"contains none of them."
msgstr ""

